   "url": "https://theosismedical.com/hacks/helpful-videos",
   "title": "Helpful Videos",
   "kind": "hack",
   "text": "11\nHelpful Videos\nHere is a repository for the videos I think are helpful for being successful in health education and management. I may have used them elsewhere already but will consolidate them all here if I can.\nWatch · Dr. Layne Norton\nHow Much Protein Is Too Much for Your Kidneys?\nHuman trials: higher protein does not harm healthy kidneys. The 1980s myth does not match the data.Watch on YouTube\nAlso on One Gram Per Pound\nWatch · Alex Hormozi\nThe Alex Hormozi Diet (REVEALED)\nFive minutes. Calories from body weight and your goal, a gram of protein per pound, leftover calories spent however you want.Watch on YouTube\nAlso on Where to Start\nWatch · Alex Hormozi\nThe Alex Hormozi Cookbook [REVEALED]\nTwelve zero-prep high-protein assemblies. Yogurt and cereal, lox on Ezekiel, tuna-yogurt, shrimp, cauliflower beef, bro nachos, egg whites. I stole the list and put the recipes on Regular Food Hacks.Watch on YouTube\nAlso on Regular Food Hacks\nWatch · Dr. Layne Norton · Biolayne\nArtificial Sweeteners are Toxic?\nA short, evidence-first look at the scare headlines. Human trials do not show the harm that petri-dish and mega-dose animal studies get shared as. This is why diet pop stays on the drink list.Watch on YouTube\nAlso on Don't Drink Calories\nWatch · Dr. Ted Naiman\nPersonal Fat Threshold\nWhy two people at different sizes can have completely different metabolic health, and why getting back under your own threshold reverses the overflow that shows up as type 2 diabetes.Watch on YouTube\nAlso on Nutritional Nerd Out\nWatch · Alila Medical Media\nAtrial Fibrillation Anatomy, ECG and Stroke, Animation.\nThree minutes: how the atria quiver instead of squeezing, what that looks like on an ECG, and how a clot from the left atrial appendage can travel to the brain.Watch on YouTube\nAlso on What Is AFib?\n10 Nutritional Nerd Out12 Reading List, Stolen With Love"
