   "url": "https://theosismedical.com/hacks/staples",
   "title": "Regular Food Hacks",
   "kind": "hack",
   "text": "07\nRegular Food Hacks\nStolen from Alex Hormozi\nKeep these in the house so the right choice is an easy choice.\nWhen I’m on the wagon and not being a hypocrite — doing the 80% of things that keep my overall health under control — these are the staples I’m rotating through.\nBetween these foods and the periodic “healthy-adjacent” takeout splurges, I’m able to stay sane while getting through a busy day to day. Diets fail when the healthier options require a 12-step recipe and the fatty liver with a side of fries option is a drive-through away. The move is to make the high-protein thing the thing you can grab while you are tired and hangry.\nThis is not a meal plan. It is a fridge that does not fight you. Hitting the × 10 rule is the ideal. Close still counts.\nIf a sweet tooth shows up: a Legendary pastry with fat-free Reddi-wip takes the cake… literally and figuratively. Like it’s really, really good.\nAnd then I stole the grocery-aisle recipes from the same jacked business YouTuber as Where to Start. Zero prep. High protein. His versions often land around 80–100 g of protein in one sitting — scale them to your number. The macros below are from the video plus typical labels. Brands move. If the numbers are on the package, trust those.\nHolwey stolen Hormozi High Protein Hacks\nYup...I once again stole from business bro. He has hacked his health heavily...you can too! See below...Watch on YouTube: The Alex Hormozi Cookbook [REVEALED]\nWatch · Alex Hormozi\nThe Alex Hormozi Cookbook [REVEALED]\nZero-prep high-protein assemblies. The recipes below are the grocery-aisle version of that video.Watch on YouTube\n01 of 11\n01\nFruity Pebbles yogurt bowl\nStir Crystal Light into 0% Greek yogurt. Keep the cereal on top so it stays crunchy. Do not mix it in.\nFage 0% Greek yogurt, ~32 oz tub\n1 packet Crystal Light (fruit punch / berry)\n½–1 cup Fruity Pebbles on top — or a high-protein cereal\nGhost protein cereal is a good swap here. About 17–18 g of protein per serving versus about 1 g in Fruity Pebbles, similar crunch if you keep it on top. Premier Protein cereal lives in the same neighborhood. Macros below are for the Fruity Pebbles version.\nCalories550\nProtein83 g\nCarbs / Fat54 g / 2 g\n% protein60%\n02\nPremier Protein cereal + Fairlife\nCereal in a bowl. High-protein milk on it. That is the whole recipe.\nPremier Protein cereal, 3 cups — or Ghost protein cereal\nFairlife ultra-filtered milk or Core Power, ~16 oz\nGhost works here too. Slightly less protein per cup than Premier, still a real protein cereal instead of dessert with a crunch.\nCalories700\nProtein90 g\nCarbs / Fat80 g / 12 g\n% protein51%\n03\nChocolate egg whites\nLiquid egg whites + zero-sugar Hershey’s syrup. Drink it, or microwave it until it puffs.\nLiquid egg whites, ~3 cups (about a carton and a half)\nZero-sugar Hershey’s syrup, 1–2 tbsp\nCalories270\nProtein54 g\nCarbs / Fat8 g / 0 g\n% protein80%\n10\nLean beef + riced cauliflower\nMicrowave a bag of riced cauliflower. Brown extra-lean beef or turkey. Sauce: light mayo"
